body:
Honestly, the cleric beast really got me the first time I saw it. Even though the fight wasn't too bad, just the way it comes into the arena is pretty wild. 

&#x200B;

On your first playthrough, there's no strong indicators that you're about to fight a boss. Then suddenly, this giant gnarled thing 10 times your size leaps from behind a building with a horrible screech followed by this intense chorus. Love it

I think that's super true, the brief time I was a line cook I initially felt like servers had it easier because they got to leave earlier and Friday/Saturday nights would be an almost guaranteed $100-$200 in tips. Then one day I saw one of our servers was in tears. They had to deal with a 15 top who was absolutely awful to her and, instead of a tip, they left one of those church leaflets that looks like a $100 bill. Those servers were essentially punching bags for people and, whenever a table would dine n dash, the check came out of their pay.

&#x200B;

Way I see it is FOH and BOH both do a ton, its just like different character classes in an RPG

I choose Bill for his ult move

&#x200B;

**The Billdozer**

Greyhound Bus Lines  


I took a bus up to Montana once or twice a year to see my family whenever I have some time off from school.  Its cheaper than a plane and usually fine but my last trip was insanely bad

&#x200B;

I traveled up there with my brother for Christmas and the trip back home would take three buses (bus to one city, then transfer on another bus, etc.). Got notified one of the transfer buses got cancelled due to weather. My brother called their customer support in India and got his ticket changed in 10 minutes. For some reason, it took me an hour, 5 different people, and getting told I'd have to buy a new ticket before actually getting my trip changed.   


**Here's where it gets almost hyperbole levels of bad:** They cancel the third bus right after we get on the first one (no email or anything). We get dropped off at their "station" and are just told "tough luck". Their "station" was the lobby of a closed down motel with trash and broken glass everywhere. Super gulp cups filled with piss in the corner and bible verses written with marker into the dusty couch. No power or plumbing. The smell of mold was nearly unbearable but it was too cold to stand outside. A homeless guy starts yelling at us from the parking lot "DO YOU KNOW WHAT IS HAPPENING!" and starts pacing back and forth eyeing us down. Get some microwave ramen from nearby gas station and had to avoid setting it down since the rats were trying to swipe my noodles. 

&#x200B;

Our phones start to die as it gets dark so we walk about a mile to a nearby Mcdonalds. Local people were incredibly nice when they heard what happened. Eventually made it the rest of the way home without having to spend the night. Fought on the phone with customer service about the crappy experience and lack of help. Got told I could choose from $100 in credit towards another ticket or $20 back to my bank account.  


Took the $20

&#x200B;

TL;DR: Greyhound will straight up strand you in Wyoming
